+### Local app (Windows)
+
+Windows users can run the local app via `app/scripts/dev.ps1` after
+`pip install -e ".[app]"`. See `install.md` for full Windows setup
+(ffmpeg via winget, skill junction, and launch).
+
+
 ## How it works
 
 The LLM never watches the video. It **reads** it ΓÇö through two layers that together give it everything it needs to cut with word-boundary precision.
 
 <p align="center">
   <img src="static/timeline-view.svg" alt="timeline_view composite ΓÇö filmstrip + speaker track + waveform + word labels + silence-gap cut candidates" width="100%">
 </p>
 
 **Layer 1 ΓÇö Audio transcript (always loaded).** One ElevenLabs Scribe call per source gives word-level timestamps, speaker diarization, and audio events (`(laughter)`, `(applause)`, `(sigh)`). All takes pack into a single ~12KB `takes_packed.md` ΓÇö the LLM's primary reading view.
 
